t is small, there is no need to bloat the pot or bluff. Taking the free card to try and hit the straight on the River or get to a cheap showdown is the optimal low-risk strategy.\n\nReason: Checking allows me to realize my equity (straight draw) for free and keeps the pot small, which aligns with protecting my cumulative lead and managing the risks posed by the wet board (flush/straight potential).\n\nAnswer: 0'}
